    "tutorTips": {
      "title": "💡 Tutor Tips | M2 Q2",
      "html": "<p class=\"aa-method\"><strong>Step 1</strong></p><p>When you are asked to analyse risks to data integrity and evaluate their impact on management’s ability to design and implement an effective strategy:</p><p>You should begin with identifying risks to data integrity when you are reading the scenario.</p><p>You should then analyse the risk by thinking of its implications. You need to think of the problems that risk would cause for data integrity. For example, could it lead to data being lost or changed without authorisation? Or maybe it could affect the accuracy of data?</p><p>When asked to evaluate the impact of the risks on the organisation’s strategy, think about the impact of unreliable data on the company’s ability to make proper decisions. For example, would it affect reports that are used for decision making or information that is published for stakeholders or regulatory compliance?</p><p class=\"aa-method\"><strong>Step 2</strong></p><p>When you are asked to analyse information given in the scenario to highlight any concerns over the accuracy, validity and completeness of the underlying data:</p><p>You need to begin by identifying the issue from the scenario and then analyse it.</p><p>It is important to read the information provided carefully. Look for unusual trends or information that appears to contradict other information and explain them.</p><p class=\"aa-method\"><strong>Step 3</strong></p><p>When you are asked to describe any further audit evidence (or procedures) that are required to conclude on whether reliance can be placed on the underlying data by the audit team:</p><p>When explaining evidence (or procedures), ensure that you identify the source document and then go on to explain what you are confirming from the source document.</p><p>If you are asked within a question to &quot;conclude&quot; on whether the audit team should place reliance on the data, make sure you include a conclusion in your answer as there will be marks in the solution allocated to this.</p>"
    },
